# O'Pip Stage-2 Independent Research & Risk Review (IRR) shadow worker
# Dedicated, bounded, non-overlapping consumer for the IRR advisory queue.
# This is NOT the protected unified cycle: it runs as its own process on the one
# scheduler (cron) and never takes the unified-cycle lock, so a slow or hung
# provider can never delay or skip a protection cycle, a scan, a Chief review or
# a Telegram delivery.
#
# Producer: the scan appends immutable evidence AFTER the final deterministic
# target, economic and portfolio/capital gates, with a bounded local append and
# no network I/O. This worker is the only process that calls the provider.
#
# Dark by default: OPIP_IRR_MODE=off (the default) makes this an inert recorded
# no-op that spends nothing. A pass is bounded to OPIP_IRR_DRAIN_BATCH requests
# (default 2, max 5), one attempt each with no retry, and every attempt reserves
# its worst-case spend before the call.
#
# NOT INSTALLABLE YET -- activation requires BOTH of the following, and this
# file stays out of the approved scheduler allowlist
# (deploy/remote/reconcile-scheduler.sh) until an owner-authorized change adds
# it, so a deploy neither installs nor removes this entry:
#
#   1. Scheduler authorization. reconcile-scheduler.sh installs this entry only
#      when the root-owned authorization marker
#      /var/lib/ohm-deploy/irr-shadow-scheduler.enabled contains exactly
#      `installed`. With no marker (the default) it installs nothing and removes
#      any previously installed entry; any other content fails closed.
#   2. Memory isolation. The worker runs as the isolated `opip-irr-shadow`
#      Compose service (profile `irr-shadow`, mem_limit 96m, read_only, cap_drop
#      ALL, no env_file, only ./data/irr mounted) and never `exec`s into the core
#      container's 384 MB cgroup. The in-container `timeout` (150s) lives in the
#      service command, so a hung provider is terminated inside that cgroup.
#
# Non-overlap: host `flock -n` plus the in-container consumer lock. Bounds: one
# batch per pass (OPIP_IRR_DRAIN_BATCH, max 5), one bounded attempt per request,
# and stale queue requests are refused before any paid call.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

* * * * * root flock -n /var/run/opip-irr-shadow.lock -c 'cd /opt/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1 && /usr/bin/docker compose --profile irr-shadow run --rm --no-deps -T opip-irr-shadow >> /var/log/opip-irr-shadow.log 2>&1'

